    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d262">

                <pb facs="0713" n="683" sameAs="frus:frus1949v01/pg683"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">560.AL/5–2149: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chairman of the United States Delegation</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Willoughby</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Annecy</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-05-21T19:00:00+01:00">May 21, 1949—7 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>139. For Brown. Work of Contracting Parties has been proceeding slowly past week
                    and can avoid raising MFN issue immediate future
                        (Deptel 120, May 19). Effort to defer
                    till end conference would, however, be strongly resisted because top personnel
                    several delegations will leave when GATT agenda
                    concluded leaving only tariff negotiations personnel here. Contemplated that
                    last Annecy meetings would be concerned mainly formalities and arrangements
                    third tariff negotiations avoiding important substantive matters.</p>
                <p>Wish to avoid taking matter up with Acting Chairman Blankenstein but will consult
                        Wilgress<anchor n="1" xml:id="d262-f1"/> upon his return in one week.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Willoughby</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d262-f1" n="1" xml:id="d262-f1-content">
                <p>L. D. Wilgress of Canada was Chairman of the Contracting Parties.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
